const content="<article data-editorial-version=\"3\" class=\"sn-page\"><div class=\"sn-read\"><a href=\"/supporters/\">← Featured sponsors</a><p class=\"sn-kicker\">Marine Diesel Engine · Sponsor feature</p><img class=\"sn-logo\" src=\"/images/supporters/honu/logo.webp\" alt=\"Honu Paddleboards logo\" width=\"210\" height=\"100\"><h1>Honu: lightweight paddleboards for enjoying your anchorage</h1><p class=\"sn-intro\">Honu makes Australian-designed inflatable paddleboards for relaxed outings, touring and surf. For boat owners, a portable board can add another activity at suitable stops without requiring permanent storage for a rigid SUP.</p><img class=\"sn-hero\" src=\"/images/supporters/honu/paddling.webp\" alt=\"Honu paddleboarding lifestyle photograph\" width=\"1000\" height=\"654\"><section><h2>Bring a board you want to use</h2><p>Honu focuses on light weight and rigidity, using woven construction and reinforcement as part of its design approach. Lower-profile designs within the range bring the rider closer to the water.</p><p>We like that the benefits connect to the whole outing. A board has to be carried and prepared before it can be enjoyed, so manageable weight matters alongside how it paddles. The inflatable format also makes packing it between trips more practical.</p></section><section><h2>Choose around the paddling</h2><p>The range includes all-round boards, touring shapes and surf SUPs, with paddles, pumps, bags, fins and accessories available too. These choices let owners consider a setup for their preferred activity rather than buying a board solely because it fits in a locker.</p><p>Honu began in Bondi in 2001 and designs in Sydney. Industrial engineer Mark Travers took over in 2019, bringing that experience to the company&#x27;s product work.</p></section><section><h2>Why we feature Honu here</h2><p>Engine maintenance is part of getting a boat ready to enjoy, and a paddleboard can make a stay at a suitable destination more enjoyable. It has a different job from the vessel&#x27;s machinery, but a useful place in a boating holiday.</p><p>We feature Honu for its clear design priorities and range of paddling options. Portability, attention to stiffness and equipment for different outings give owners practical reasons to consider bringing a board along.</p></section><div class=\"sn-contact\"><a href=\"https://honuboards.com/en-au\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"sponsored nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Explore Honu paddleboards ↗</a><a href=\"/supporters/\">More featured sponsors</a></div></div></article><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"Article\", \"headline\": \"Honu: lightweight paddleboards for enjoying your anchorage\", \"description\": \"Discover Honu inflatable paddleboards, with Australian design, low weight and attention to stiffness for paddling during your boating holidays.\", \"image\": \"https://marinedieselengine.com.au/images/supporters/honu/paddling.webp\", \"author\": {\"@type\": \"Organization\", \"name\": \"Marine Diesel Engine\"}, \"dateModified\": \"2026-11-05\", \"mainEntityOfPage\": \"https://marinedieselengine.com.au/supporters/honu/\"}</script>";
